PLACEHOLDER — NOT A REAL RIVE FILE.

This file exists only so Metro's static `require('./heaven-intro.riv')` in
RiveIntroScene.tsx resolves to something at build time. It intentionally
does not parse as a .riv binary: the app's error handling (useRiveFile's
`error` result, and RiveView's `onError`) treats a failed load exactly like
"Rive unavailable" and falls back to the reduced Simple intro automatically,
so this placeholder is safe to ship without breaking the build or the app.

Replace this file with the real export from the Rive editor, named exactly
`heaven-intro.riv`, built to the specification in RIVE_SPEC.md in this same
folder. No code changes should be needed if the artboard/state machine/event
names match that spec.
